{"pageId":"/pages/examples/@id","routeParams":{"id":"basic-usage"},"data":{"example":{"id":"basic-usage","title":"Getting Started","description":"Minimal setup demonstrating CLI usage and simple programmatic scanning.\nThis is the first example new users should explore.\n","rootPath":"/home/runner/work/functional-examples/functional-examples/examples/basic-usage","files":[{"absolutePath":"/home/runner/work/functional-examples/functional-examples/examples/basic-usage/README.md","relativePath":"README.md","raw":"# Getting Started\n\nThis example demonstrates the most basic use case: scanning for examples using the CLI and programmatic API.\n\n## CLI Usage\n\n```bash\n# Scan for examples\nfunctional-examples scan\n\n# Output as JSON\nfunctional-examples scan -f json\n```\n\n## Programmatic Usage\n\nThe `scan.ts` file demonstrates the simplest programmatic entry point:\n\n<%= file('scan.ts').region('scan') %>\n\nThe `scan()` function auto-discovers your config file and installed plugins, then returns:\n- `examples` — Array of extracted examples\n- `errors` — Array of any errors encountered during scanning\n- `stats` — Timing and count information\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n### JSON Configuration\n\nThis example uses a JSON config (`functional-examples.config.json`) which is the simplest way to configure scanning. Plugins are auto-detected from your `package.json` dependencies.\n\n### `scan()`\n\nThe convenience function wraps config discovery, loading, resolution, and scanning in a single call. For most use cases, this is all you need.\n","parsed":"!undefined","hunks":"!undefined","language":"markdown","highlightedHtml":"<pre class=\"shiki blueprint\" style=\"background-color:#122a48f2;color:#e8edf4\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-markdown\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">#</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> Getting Started</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">This example demonstrates the most basic use case: scanning for examples using the CLI and programmatic API.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">##</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> CLI Usage</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">```</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">bash</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6B8AAA;font-style:italic\"># Scan for examples</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B8D8F0\">functional-examples</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\"> scan</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6B8AAA;font-style:italic\"># Output as JSON</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B8D8F0\">functional-examples</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\"> scan</span><span style=\"color:#D4A94E\"> -f</span><span style=\"color:#7CC9A0\"> json</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">```</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">##</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> Programmatic Usage</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">The </span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">scan.ts</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> file demonstrates the simplest programmatic entry point:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">&#x3C;%= file('scan.ts').region('scan') %></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">The </span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">scan()</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> function auto-discovers your config file and installed plugins, then returns:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">-</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\"> `</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">examples</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> — Array of extracted examples</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">-</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\"> `</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">errors</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> — Array of any errors encountered during scanning</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">-</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\"> `</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">stats</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> — Timing and count information</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">##</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> Key Concepts</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">###</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> JSON Configuration</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">This example uses a JSON config (</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">functional-examples.config.json</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">) which is the simplest way to configure scanning. Plugins are auto-detected from your </span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">package.json</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\"> dependencies.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">###</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\"> `</span><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">scan()</span><span style=\"color:#8FA4BE\">`</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E8EDF4\">The convenience function wraps config discovery, loading, reso